# The Vivado project tinytpu_v2_zed_project/ is build output, so it is ignored as a whole. Exception (16 Nov 2026), the same as
# mac_attack_accel_MLP/zed/mac_zed_project: these parts of it ARE tracked (added with git add -f), so a teammate
# can open it, program the board and run the apps without the 10-minute build:
#   tinytpu_v2_zed_project/*.xpr, *.srcs (block design), *.runs (bitstream, checkpoints, reports), *.hw
#   tinytpu_v2_zed_project/*.sdk/<app>/.project, .cproject and src/  for each SDK application
# Not tracked (the tools remake them): caches, logs, .Xil, the SDK's .metadata, the BSP (model_v2_test_bsp),
# the hardware platform (system_wrapper_hw_platform_0), the exported .hdf and the apps' Debug/Release folders.
# A new file inside the project stays ignored until it is added with git add -f.
tinytpu_v2_zed_project/
sim/sim_build/
sim/results.xml
sim/__pycache__/
sim/cosim/build/
build_bitstream.log
sdk_build.log
sim/xsim_cosim/build_*/
.Xil/
